You are a code reviewer in a whole-repository review. Scope: correctness and regression-risk review of the edge C++ server at /home/ubuntu/个人学习/AI-powered-Network-Diagnostics/server (plus client/). STRICTLY READ-ONLY: never modify any file; do not touch openspec/, .ai-harness/, build dirs; do not run builds (x86 build and ARM64 build already verified green; 51/51 unit tests pass).

Read server.cpp (thread/plugin orchestration + ServerContext lifecycle), monitor_manager.cpp/monitor_plugins.cpp/monitor_ebpf_plugins.cpp, dbus_service.cpp, event_manager.cpp, weak_netmgr.cpp, database_manager.cpp, weaknet_config.cpp, and the newer subsystems: bt_data_path_analyzer/bt_data_path_anomaly_detector/bt_hci_connection_tracker (Phase1/2 Bluetooth HCI ACL), bt_event_monitor/bt_event_normalizer/wireless_event_store/site_incident_correlator (canonical events + incidents), edge_telemetry_exporter.cpp/edge_wireless_uplink_exporter.cpp/network_epoch_store.cpp (edge uplink), assurance/ (SLE evaluators, overall_policy, state_stabilizer), metrics/. Skim eBPF programs server/src/*.bpf.c and server/src/bpf/*.bpf.c for map sizing/ABI mismatches against their userspace readers (there is a recently archived change ebpf-map-sizing-wiring — check openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-27-ebpf-map-sizing-wiring/ design/evaluation for known fixed issues, read-only).

Hunt for REAL defects with concrete failure scenarios, prioritized:
- data races / missing locks on shared state across monitor threads, D-Bus dispatch thread, edge uplink thread, EventManager signal thread (note documented design: iface_mutex, mutable mutexes);
- lifecycle bugs: stop()/join ordering, use-after-free of ServerContext members, eBPF map fd leaks, thread not stopped on Looper exit;
- integer/size mismatches between BPF map value structs and userspace structs; endianness (bdaddr_t is reverse-order — documented); signedness of RSSI/reason codes;
- SQLite concurrency (single-writer rule), error paths that silently swallow failures (documented known trap: DatabaseManager failed-to-open produces no persistent errors — is the current code still like that?);
- edge uplink correctness: cursor advancement only on 2xx, network_epoch persistence, signing over exact bytes, idempotency key construction;
- Bluetooth HCI: handle==0 filtering, generation isolation, dead-handle cleanup, reason-code domain mixing (mgmt vs HCI) — verify the fixes documented in docs/蓝牙监控优化实现方案.md §11 actually exist in code;
- off-by-one / window logic in assurance evaluators (missingness 三态, SR-9 critical burst, StateStabilizer holds);
- error handling: unchecked return codes that lead to UB, buffer overflows in fixed-size char arrays (e.g. source_detail 32), snprintf truncation.

For each finding: file:line, what breaks, concrete trigger scenario, severity (Critical/Important/Minor), and a suggested fix direction (do NOT implement). Verify each finding against the actual code before reporting — read the surrounding code, don't grep-match and assume. Cross-check against existing unit tests in server/test/ to note whether a test already guards it (if so, downgrade or drop). Only report findings you are confident are real. Order by severity. Also list 3-5 things you checked that look solid (so the report shows coverage).

